This week in Science, I learned about isotopes, the periodic table, and atomic structure.
I learned how to identify which elements are metals and non-metals, and how elements are organised into different groups in the periodic table. I also learned that elements in the same group can have similar properties.
We also reviewed the rules for atomic number and mass number. The atomic number tells me the number of protons, and in a neutral atom it also tells me the number of electrons. The mass number is the total number of protons plus neutrons.
I also learned about isotopes. Isotopes are atoms of the same element, so they have the same number of protons, but they can have different numbers of neutrons. This means they have the same atomic number but different mass numbers.
The main idea I learned this week is that the periodic table is not just a list of elements. The position of an element, its group, and its atomic structure can help explain its properties and how it behaves.
